                  "args": {
                    "path": "report/sections/summary.md",
                    "content": "This paper introduces Feature 3DGS, a method that extends 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) to support arbitrary-dimensional semantic feature fields via distillation from 2D foundation models like SAM and CLIP-LSeg [source: text.md L87-L117]. It overcomes limitations of prior NeRF-based feature field methods—namely slow rendering and continuity artifacts—by leveraging the real-time rendering speed of 3DGS while enabling novel-view semantic segmentation, language-guided editing, and promptable segmentation (e.g., \"segment anything\") [source: text.md L75-L127]. The authors claim their method is faster to train and render than NeRF-based alternatives and, to their knowledge, the first to enable point and bounding-box prompting for radiance field manipulation using SAM [source: text.md L119-L127]."
