                {
                  "tool": "write_file",
                  "args": {
                    "path": "report/sections/methodology.md",
                    "content": "Feature 3DGS extends the 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) framework by associating a semantic feature vector with each 3D Gaussian, in addition to its standard color and opacity attributes [source: text.md L219-L221]. The core technical innovation is a \"Parallel N-dimensional Gaussian Rasterizer\" that differentiably splats and rasterizes these high-dimensional feature vectors, enabling distillation from 2D foundation models like SAM and CLIP-LSeg [source: text.md L359-L365, L225-L227].\n\nTo address the computational bottleneck of high-dimensional features, the method employs a two-stage strategy: it first learns a structured, lower-dimensional feature field and then applies a lightweight convolutional decoder to upsample it to the target dimension during rasterization [source: text.md L237-L241]. This design allows for fast training and rendering while preserving feature quality. The framework is general and compatible with various 2D foundation models, and it also introduces point and bounding-box prompting capabilities for radiance field manipulation by leveraging the SAM model [source: text.md L124-L127, L263-L267]."
                  }
                },
                {
                  "tool": "grep",
                  "args": {
