                  "tool": "read_file",
                  "args": {
                    "path": "C:\\Users\\13970\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-08-18\\https-github-com-abigailorz-paperwise-git\\work\\PaperWise\\workspace\\benchmarks\\eval_workspace\\eval_runs\\report_generation_1787746207_0\\paper\\text.md",
                    "offset": 937,
                    "limit": 500
                  }
                },
                {
                  "tool": "write_file",
                  "args": {
                    "path": "report/sections/experiments.md",
                    "content": "The experiments demonstrate that Feature 3DGS achieves superior performance and speed compared to the NeRF-based baseline NeRF-DFF. On the Replica dataset, Feature 3DGS achieves an mIoU of 0.787 (vs. 0.636 for NeRF-DFF) and an accuracy of 0.943 (vs. 0.864), while also being significantly faster: its inference is 1.66× faster than NeRF-DFF when rendering 128-dimensional features [source: text.md L977, L1041, L1043, L1049, L1051]. With the optional \"speed-up module,\" the frame rate increases to 14.55 FPS, more than double the 6.84 FPS of the full model, without sacrificing RGB rendering quality (PSNR: 37.012 vs. 36.915) [source: text.md L991, L1037, L1041, L1083-L1091]. Qualitatively, Feature 3DGS produces more fine-grained segmentation masks and cleaner language-guided edits (e.g., extracting a banana hidden behind an apple) with fewer background floaters than NeRF-DFF [source: text.md L979, L1271-L1275, L1379-L1381]."
                  }
                },
